   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_uncoded",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF describes its samples only as text with no ontology term, so the curated organism part, cell type, disease and individual columns are empty. The text is in sample_characteristics: organism part: Ependymal cell. Match on it as text; it has not been mapped to a term."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 190 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "1 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: Trypsin Digested:GG (Ubiquitination Site) on K. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "no_output_sdrf",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "The search did not write an SDRF back out, so sample metadata comes from the deposited SDRF only. Producer's note: no reanalysis SDRF written (WriteSdrf is MetaMorpheus #2816, unreleased)"
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "208 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   }
